  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Title: Training and Mentoring Women and Youth SMEs on business continuity during a pandemic Implementing Partner: Kenya Private Sector Alliance (KEPSA). The objective of the project is to give developing SMEs access to training, mentorship, investors (financing) and other support to help them become more stable, self-sufficient businesses. This project builds upon gains of trainings and mentorship services that the Irish Embassy supported in 2020. Current project takes the model of a business accelerator targeting three cohorts of 50 SMEs each for 4 months. To bridge the gender gap, KEPSA will also ensure that the program targets women-led and youth-led businesses.  Activities: This programme gives developing SMEs access to training, mentorship, investors (Financing) and other support that help them become more stable, self-sufficient businesses</narrative>
  </description>
